※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4213

※ A lambda that does not say it lasts is not given where one that does is
※ wanted, even where the compiler could have kept it in `⎕heap`: the program
※ says so, `[n] in ⎕heap`, and a value already made may be in a frame.

fn keep(f: fn(u8) in ⎕heap → u8) → fn(u8) in ⎕heap → u8:
    f

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 1u8
    let p: fn(u8) → u8 = λ x: u8 [n] → u8 { x + n }
    let q: fn(u8) in ⎕heap → u8 = keep(p)
    if q(1u8) = 2u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
